# WC26 Bracket Architecture

## Stack
- Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind 4
- Client state: `localStorage` (predictions, group scores, ranking, bolão)
- Share: JWT tokens via `jose` (`/api/share`, `/b/[hash]`)
- Optional live data: API-Football via `/api/matches`

## Data Flow
1. Static seed data in `src/data/` synced from [worldcup26.ir](https://worldcup26.ir) (teams, matches, stadiums)
2. Sync script (`npm run sync:worldcup`) enriches seed with API fields: `flagUrl`, `iso2`, `apiId`, stadium/time/scorers/labels
3. Live scores via `/api/matches`, `/api/groups` (worldcup26.ir, 30s cache); client merges API overlay onto static seed
4. User edits group scores → merged into `liveMatches`
5. `resolveFullBracket(predictions, liveMatches)` → knockout tree with `fixture?: Match` per slot
6. `calculateScore(predictions, resultMatches)` → points
7. Share token encodes predictions for `/b/[hash]`

## API-Enriched Local Seed Data
- `Team.flag` emoji kept as fallback; `Team.flagUrl` from flagcdn.com when synced
- `TeamFlag` component (`next/image` + emoji fallback) used in bracket UI and group tables
- `Match` optional fields: `apiId`, `time`, `stadiumId`, `persianDate`, scorers, knockout labels
- `buildKnockoutFixtureMap()` maps `r32-1`…`final` → real fixtures for display only; predictions still drive advancement
- Live matches: `status: "live"` with partial scores; standings count only `finished`

## Local-First Limits
- No database or auth; ranking/bolão are per-browser only
- Share links are read-only; import into local ranking/bolão manually
- Live data from worldcup26.ir (free, no API key); falls back to static seed on error
- Re-sync static data: `npm run sync:worldcup`
- Squad data: `npm run sync:squads` → `src/data/squads.json` (26×48); validate with `npm run check:players`
- **projetoCopa catalog**: when `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_*` is set, `/api/matches` merges live scores from Supabase (`football_fixtures`); `/api/catalog/teams` and `/api/catalog/fixtures` expose read-only catalog
- UI language: client-side `pt-BR` (default) or `en-US` via header toggle; persisted in `localStorage` key `wc26-locale`; no locale-prefixed routes

## Squad Data (Draft / Campaign)
- `squads.json` — per-nation roster of 26 `SquadPlayerSeed` entries (name, position, rating, shirtNumber, role, club?)
- `players.ts` — builds `Player[]` with ids; `getPlayersByTeam()` returns sorted squad
- `sync-squads.mjs` — API-Football `/players/squads` (if `API_FOOTBALL_KEY`), Wikipedia WC squad tables, legacy seed padding
- `position-map.ts` — API/Wikipedia position strings → draft enum; `compareSquadPlayers()` for call-up order

